Bleach ( bleach.jp)  is a Japanese manga created and written by Tite Kubo; it initially began serialization in Shueisha's Monthly Shonen Jump between January and June 2002. The first compiled book was released on September 19th, 2003. ^{[1]} Published in other countries it has been serialized in several magazines such as Anime Magazine and Young Saturday. It won the Kodansha Award for Shounen titles for 2005 ^{[2]}
It tells of Ichigo Kurosaki ("Blade"), an orphan destined to become a Soul Reaper. As such he can use spiritual energy from souls -the dead and dying to carry out his missions. On his quest, he discovers Soul Society and its rule in a dark battle in which both Ichigo and Soul Reaper Yoruichi are hurt. He becomes lost in this surreal world. During Ichigo's so called "missing time" Yoruichi has visited him. Yoru
